{# The frame response for an account the user has just expanded. The rows are
   shared with the sidebar's own inline render — see _account_folder_rows.

   `frameId` rather than a literal: the desktop rail and the mobile drawer each
   render a frame for this account and they cannot share an id, so the reply has
   to wear whichever one asked. MailController::folderFrameId() decides, and
   only ever returns one of the two. #}
<turbo-frame id="{{ frameId|default('account-folders-' ~ account.id) }}">
    {% include 'mail/_account_folder_rows.html.twig' with { account: account, labels: labels } only %}
</turbo-frame>
